## 1. Admin Levels & Role System

### What the boss wants
- 1 Super Admin who controls everything
- Different admin levels
- User types: Admin, Screener, User, etc.

### What exists today
- Only 2 roles: `applicant` and `admin` (stored in `profiles.role`)
- Single admin check: `role === 'admin'`

### 💡 How to implement

**Expand the role system to 5 tiers:**

| Role | Access Level | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `super_admin` | 🔴 Full | God mode. Can manage other admins, view audit logs, configure the platform, manage all settings |
| `hr_admin` | 🟠 High | Full HR access. Review applicants, schedule interviews, manage exams, send emails, view all data |
| `screener` | 🟡 Medium | Can ONLY view & filter new applications, mark as qualified/disqualified, add notes. Cannot hire or manage settings |
| `agent` | 🟢 Low | A hired agent. Access to training portal, their own contract, performance dashboard |
| `applicant` | ⚪ Basic | Can apply, take exams, view their own status. This is what exists today |

**Database change:**
```sql
ALTER TABLE public.profiles 
  DROP CONSTRAINT profiles_role_check,
  ADD CONSTRAINT profiles_role_check 
    CHECK (role IN ('applicant', 'screener', 'hr_admin', 'super_admin', 'agent'));
```

**New files needed:**
- `src/lib/permissions.ts` — Central permission map (e.g. `canViewApplicants`, `canHireAgent`, `canManageAdmins`)
- `src/middleware.ts` — Enhanced route protection per role
- `src/app/admin/team/page.tsx` — Super Admin page to manage staff accounts & assign roles

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Super Admin account:** Only 1 super_admin should exist. Created manually via Supabase SQL console. The platform should NOT have a signup form for admins — the Super Admin invites them via email.

