## 2. Applicant Login — Do They Need One?

### 🤔 My Recommendation: YES, but make it seamless

Here's why and how:

| Approach | Pros | Cons |
|---|---|---|
| **No login** (anonymous form) | Simpler UX | Can't track applicant status, can't do exams, can't show dashboard, can't send them back to check progress |
| **Login after apply** ✅ (current) | Applicants get a dashboard, can take exams, check status, upload more docs | Extra step during application |
| **Magic link login** (my recommendation) | No password to remember, ultra-modern, secure | Requires email infrastructure |

**My recommendation:** Keep the current approach (create account during application) BUT add these improvements:

1. **Magic Link option** — After first application, let them log back in via email magic link (no password needed)
2. **Application tracking page** — `/track?email=xxx` public page where they enter email to get a status update (no login required)
3. **Password is optional** — During application, auto-generate a password or use magic link only

> [!TIP]
> The current system already creates a Supabase auth account during application. This is the right pattern. The applicant can log in later to check their status at `/dashboard`.

